       "endIndex": 411,
       "text": "While the headline number looks appealing due to Google\u2019s front-loaded equity structure, the initial offer takes a step backward on your base salary and leaves significant money on the table for an L6 (Staff / Senior PM) role"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
       0,
       1
      ]
     },
     {
      "segment": {
       "startIndex": 498,
       "endIndex": 594,
       "text": "Google uses a front-loaded **33% / 33% / 22% / 12%** vesting schedule for new-hire equity grants"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
       2,
       3,
       4
      ]
     },
     {
      "segment": {
       "startIndex": 1248,
       "endIndex": 1377,
       "text": "**Year 1 & 2 Upside:** You get a healthy **+$112k/yr bump** over your Meta comp for the first two years due to the 33% front-load"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
       3,
       4
      ]
     },
     {
      "segment": {
       "startIndex": 1538,
       "endIndex": 1686,
       "text": "**Missing Sign-on Bonus:** For external L6 PM hires\u2014especially passive candidates being poached from Meta\u2014a first-year sign-on bonus is standard"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
       0
      ]
     },
     {
      "segment": {
       "startIndex": 1690,
       "endIndex": 1787,
       "text": "**Year 3 & 4 Cliff:** Google\u2019s initial grant drops sharply in Year 3 ($238k) and Year 4 ($130k)"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
       3,
       4
      ]
     },
     {
      "segment": {
       "startIndex": 1789,
       "endIndex": 1885,
       "text": "Google relies on annual refreshers (which typically vest 25%/yr over 4 years) to bridge this gap"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
       4,
       5
      ]
     },
     {
      "segment": {
       "startIndex": 1789,
       "endIndex": 2013,
       "text": "Google relies on annual refreshers (which typically vest 25%/yr over 4 years) to bridge this gap, but because refreshers depend entirely on performance ratings and calibration, you should secure more upfront guaranteed value"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
       3
      ]
     },
     {
      "segment": {
       "startIndex": 2136,
       "endIndex": 2301,
       "text": "Your goal is to increase base salary to avoid a pay cut, secure a sign-on bonus to bridge transition friction, and push the equity grant toward top-of-band L6 levels"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
       0
      ]
     },
     {
      "segment": {
       "startIndex": 2563,
       "endIndex": 2723,
       "text": "| **Sign-On Bonus** | $0 | **$75,000 \u2013 $100,000** | Offsets leaving your stable pipeline of Meta refreshers and forfeiting unvested equity/annual bonus cycles"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
       0
      ]
     },
     {
      "segment": {
       "startIndex": 2727,
       "endIndex": 2851,
       "text": "| **Equity (GSUs)** | $1,080,000 / 4 yrs | **$1,250,000 \u2013 $1,300,000 / 4 yrs** | Standard top-tier band for Bay Area L6 PM"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
       0
      ]
     },
     {
      "segment": {
       "startIndex": 2853,
       "endIndex": 2892,
       "text": "At $1.25M, Year 1 equity becomes ~$412k"
      },
